  "result": "DONE: Research confirms project folder separation aligns with industry best practices for monorepo organization, git worktree isolation, and separation of concerns.\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n1. **Monorepo standard pattern**: Modern 2026 best practices recommend `/apps` and `/libs` directories to separate project-specific code from reusable/shared code - directly supporting `studio/` vs `projects/` separation ([Mindful Chase - Monorepo Best Practices](https://mindfulchase.com/deep-dives/monorepo-fundamentals-deep-dives-into-unified-codebases/structuring-your-monorepo-best-practices-for-directory-and-code-organization.html))\n\n2. **Git worktree enablement**: Isolated project folders enable worktrees with \"private HEAD, private index, private working directory\" - described as \"single highest-impact change\" for parallel agent work ([MindStudio - Git Worktrees for AI Coding](https://www.mindstudio.ai/blog/git-worktrees-parallel-ai-coding-agents))\n\n3. **Separation of concerns principle**: Folder boundaries create maintainability - \"singularity of purpose of individual components render the system easier to maintain\" ([DevIQ - Separation of Concerns](https://deviq.com/principles/separation-of-concerns/))\n\n4. **Clean generated/source split**: Industry practice separates generated artifacts from source code in distinct directories ([GeeksforGeeks - Separation of Concerns](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/software-engineering/separation-of-concerns-soc/))\n\n5. **Minimal overhead**: Worktrees share `.git` object database - \"only working-directory files are duplicated\" so isolation costs minimal disk space ([Zylos Research - Worktree Isolation Patterns](https://zylos.ai/research/2026-02-22-git-worktree-parallel-ai-development/))\n\n**Recommendation**: Codify pattern. Consider adding to project creation tooling.",
