  "result": "DONE: role.md IS re-injected every message, but this is mitigated by Claude's prompt caching (5x cost reduction after first turn).\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n1. **Yes, role.md is sent every message**: `agent.py:77` passes `system_prompt` to backend \u2192 `claude_cli.py:106-107` injects it into every prompt\n\n2. **Session persistence \u2260 system prompt persistence**: `--resume` preserves conversation history, but system_prompt is still re-sent each API call (by design in Claude's API)\n\n3. **Mitigated by prompt caching**: After first message, identical system prompts get `cache_read_input_tokens` pricing (90% cheaper). This is why metrics show cache hits.\n\n4. **Role.md already optimized**: Tasks T397-T400 trimmed roles to <1000 chars each. At ~200 tokens per injection, cost is ~$0.0006/message with caching.\n\n5. **Breaking change if \"fixed\"**: Removing per-message injection would require session-aware state management and break stateless backend architecture.\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n\n| Option | Pros | Cons |\n|--------|------|------|\n| Keep current (inject every msg) | Works with caching, stateless | Slight redundancy |\n| Inject only first message | Save ~200 tokens | Breaks on session reset, complex state |\n| Move to native Claude system_prompt | Cleaner separation | Still re-sent by Claude CLI architecture |\n\n**Recommendation**: No change needed. Current design is correct - prompt caching already provides the optimization. The ~200 tokens of role.md are negligible vs. the 10k+ tokens of conversation context.",
